      "created_at": "2016-02-01T03:02:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So TimCosing <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/127893#comment-127893\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">provided</a> us with some more puzzles we haven't solved yet:</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"PeterCHaward\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n PeterCHaward:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<ul><li> Worked out what the other sound clips were </li><li> Worked out what the coloring of \"intervene\" meant (hint: it's not an additional key - it was actually intended to point towards the eventual solution of that image) </li><li> Noticed the logic of which characters were included in&nbsp; <a href=\"http://greaterthangames.com/445566778Spotted\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://greaterthangames.com/445566778</a></li><li>Spotted &nbsp;that the FT ADAMANT ascii art was exactly 128 characters on each line (thus the footnote in the comic)\n</li></ul></blockquote>\n</aside>\n \n ​I don't know exactly what all of these are referring to, but I'll start with one I got involved in: the characters at&nbsp; <a href=\"http://greaterthangames.com/445566778Spotted\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://greaterthangames.com/445566778</a>&nbsp;are\n<ul><li>Paul Parsons (Legacy)</li><li>Tyler Vance (Bunker)</li><li>Maia Montgomery (Wraith)</li><li>Ryan Frost (Absolute Zero)</li><li>Helena (Fanatic) (end of line)</li><li>Vanessa Long (Visionary)</li><li>Aata Wakarewa (Haka)</li><li>Dr. Meredith Stinson (Tachyon)</li><li>Dr. Blake Montgomery (Ra)</li></ul>\nSo, at a glance, these are the base set heroes minus Tempest. (I think I nearly noticed this while working it out.) Why is Tempest missing here? Is it just that the apostrophe would be too much of a clue? Or is there some other significance to this set of heroes?",
