      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "So TimCosing <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/127893#comment-127893\">provided</a> us with some more puzzles we haven&#39;t solved yet:\n\n \n[quote=\"PeterCHaward\"]\n \n<ul style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\"><li> Worked out what the other sound clips were </li><li> Worked out what the coloring of &quot;intervene&quot; meant (hint: it&#39;s not an additional key - it was actually intended to point towards the eventual solution of that image) </li><li> Noticed the logic of which characters were included in&nbsp; <a href=\"http://greaterthangames.com/445566778Spotted\">http://greaterthangames.com/445566778</a></li><li>Spotted &nbsp;that the FT ADAMANT ascii art was exactly 128 characters on each line (thus the footnote in the comic)\n[/quote]\n </li></ul>\n ​I don&#39;t know exactly what all of these are referring to, but I&#39;ll start with one I got involved in: the characters at&nbsp; <a href=\"http://greaterthangames.com/445566778Spotted\" style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">http://greaterthangames.com/445566778</a>&nbsp;are\n<ul><li>Paul Parsons (Legacy)</li><li>Tyler Vance (Bunker)</li><li>Maia Montgomery (Wraith)</li><li>Ryan Frost (Absolute Zero)</li><li>Helena (Fanatic) (end of line)</li><li>Vanessa Long (Visionary)</li><li>Aata Wakarewa (Haka)</li><li>Dr. Meredith Stinson (Tachyon)</li><li>Dr. Blake Montgomery (Ra)</li></ul>\nSo, at a glance, these are the base set heroes minus Tempest. (I think I nearly noticed this while working it out.) Why is Tempest missing here? Is it just that the apostrophe would be too much of a clue? Or is there some other significance to this set of heroes?\n",
